<Editorial heading="How is strata cleaning priced?" fs="Strata cleaning prices follow building size, visit frequency and access points \u2013 written as a monthly invoice after a site audit." copy={({"heading": "How is strata cleaning priced?", "answer": "Strata cleaning prices follow **building size, visit frequency and access points** – written as a monthly invoice after a site audit.", "before": ["Building size sets the base minutes; visit frequency multiplies them across the week; access points decide whether the team services one entry or several. Amenity count, lift banks and carpark area adjust the figure inside that frame.", "Every engagement ships as a written quote first, so the owners corporation sees the rate structure before approval.", "Older walk-ups and new towers price on the same frame – stairwell count, lift banks and basement levels feed the audit, and committees compare like-for-like written quotes rather than hourly guesses.", "Buyers who ask about an hourly rate find it folded into the contract figure – the monthly invoice carries wages, super and insurance, then stays flat until scope changes."], "items": [], "list_ordered": false, "qa": [], "links": [], "after": []})} brand="Whistle Clean" logo="/logo.svg" />
